p.src:
Delta normalization fixes the constant: $\psi_p(x)
=
\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\hbar}}e^{ipx/\hbar}.$ Indeed, $\begin{aligned}
\braket{p'}{p}
&=
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}
dx\,
\psi_{p'}^*(x)\psi_p(x) \notag\\
&=
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}
\frac{dx}{2\pi\hbar}
e^{i(p-p')x/\hbar} \notag\\
&=
\delta(p-p').
\end{aligned}$ After choosing units with $\hbar=1$, these formulas become $\psi_p(x)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{ipx},
\qquad
\int\frac{dx}{2\pi}e^{i(p-p')x}
=\delta(p-p').$

